<title>HONG KONG: SE Asian traffic now biggest in HKG air imports.</title>
<headline>SE Asian traffic now biggest in HKG air imports.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South East Asia was the most important region for goods handled at Hong Kong in Septmber with an increase of nearly 10 percent over year ago data, its Civil Aviation Department statistics show.</p>
<p>Canada and the U.S. remained the largest regional export market but combined exports and imports only rose 1.59 percent above September 1995.</p>
<p>In percentage terms the biggest growth was in trade with Africa which grew by over 40 percent although in absolute terms the amount was small.</p>
<p>Total cargo handled in September rose by 7.17 per cent compared with the same month last year. Air cargo imports on both scheduled and non-scheduled flights reached 60,334.68 tonnes whilst exports climbed to 79,954.08.</p>
